monitor/assert-shims-wrapped.sh	_asw_ps_list=$(ls -t "$_asw_ps_home"/shell-snapshots/snapshot-*.sh 2>/dev/null)	1	ls	/shell-snapshots/snapshot-*.sh	safe	safe (a): STRUCTURALLY IMMUNE at the site, not safe-by-reachability — REKEYED 2026-09-07 (#1477 F1): the two former `ls -t … | head -1` sites moved into `_asw_pick_snapshot`, which now walks the listing. Under nullglob an unmatched glob VANISHES and `ls -t` lists the CWD with RELATIVE names; the walk applies a per-candidate POST-CONDITION `case "$_asw_ps_f" in "$_asw_ps_home"/shell-snapshots/*) … *) continue` before any candidate is read, so a bare-`ls` listing contributes NOTHING and the leg degrades to NOT CHECKED (79). Same disposition as the rows it replaces, re-read against the new text.
